<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Sertorius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 126–73 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Sertorius was a Roman general of the Marian faction who, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>'s victory, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> his base. With Lusitanian and Celtiberian allies he defeated the Senate's commanders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-caecilius-metellus-pius">Metellus Pius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> for years, setting up his own senate and a school for Iberian nobles at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huesca">Osca</a>. He was murdered by his officer Perperna around 73 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quintus-sertorius.jpg" alt="Quintus Sertorius" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bolskan (Espagne; atelier monétaire). Atelier monétaire · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Denier,_argent,_Bolskan,_Ib%C3%A9rie_-_btv1b8482613k_(2_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The final phase came in the Sertorian War of 80–72 BCE, when the Roman rebel <b>Quintus Sertorius</b> won the support of Lusitanians and Celtiberians and resisted the armies of Quintus Caecilius Metellus Pius and Pompey for several years.</blockquote><a href="/empire/celtiberians">Celtiberians · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Their lands formed part of the Republican province of Hispania Ulterior, and campaigns by Decimus Junius Brutus in 138–137 BCE, by Julius Caesar as governor in 61–60 BCE and by others completed the conquest, interrupted by the war of <b>Sertorius</b> in the 70s BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/lusitania">Lusitania · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Arevaci later backed <b>Sertorius</b> before becoming part of Hispania Citerior.</blockquote><a href="/state/arevaci">Arevaci</a></li><li><blockquote>In 76 BCE <b>Sertorius</b> captured Vareia during his war against Rome.</blockquote><a href="/state/berones">Berones</a></li><li><blockquote>According to Jerome, around 72 BCE Pompey, returning from his war against <b>Sertorius</b> in Hispania, settled defeated fighters and mountain people at Lugdunum in the upper Garonne valley.</blockquote><a href="/state/convenae">Convenae</a></li><li><blockquote>It was the main theatre of <b>Sertorius</b>' war from 80 to 72 BCE, ended by Pompey, and of Caesar's victory at Ilerda in 49 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norcia">Norcia</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in Osca, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=42.79,13.09&amp;year=-92" aria-label="Norcia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4867 643 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Quintus Sertorius"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5317 913h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5317 913h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=42.79,13.09&amp;year=-92">What was here in 92 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
